WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.570
- And let's talk about sobriety.

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.736
You've struggled with addiction, right?

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.600
- I'll be sober for,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.399
it'll be 30 years this--

00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:09.238
(audience cheers)

00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:10.266
- Damn.

00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:12.539
- I mean if I get there.

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:13.372
- (laughs) Shut up!

00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:16.349
- If I get there, this could
have gin in it tomorrow.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.973
- (laughs) That's awesome.

00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:20.830
No, but that's hard though.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.740
And an addiction is for
many different things.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.807
- Yeah, whether it's food,
alcohol, sugar, drugs,

00:00:26.807 --> 00:00:28.430
bad relationships, whatever it is.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.660
Its like you kind of
get it together in one

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.020
and it becomes a full time job.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.260
But it changed my life.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.900
It was the best thing I ever did.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.320
It enabled me to have a solid marriage

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.710
and kids and a career.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.850
And I didn't end up a crazy actor,

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.800
which is always a possibility.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.949
- Which is always a possibility
for singers as well.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:46.808
- As we know.

00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:48.818
- Yeah, we can go (imitates cuckoo bird)

00:00:48.818 --> 00:00:50.200
- Well its definitely a possibility.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.350
- What was the final,
because I have people

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:54.232
in my life that struggle with addiction

00:00:54.232 --> 00:00:55.669
are currently going through it.

00:00:55.669 --> 00:00:56.990
Like what's your advice
for people like that?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.500
Because its such an everyday
struggle it seems like

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.333
- Well the--

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:02.810
- to break the habitual cycle.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.110
- I mean the one piece of
advice I really like to share

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.730
having raised two young men.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.890
And everybody has to
learn their relationship

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:09.723
with alcohol and drugs.

00:01:09.723 --> 00:01:10.556
Everybody has to.

00:01:10.556 --> 00:01:12.710
They have to figure out how
they are going to navigate it.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.970
And having just done that with two boys,

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.440
I like to tell parents
honestly all you can do is

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.355
try to keep them alive and--

00:01:20.355 --> 00:01:21.560
- (Kelly) It's up to them.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.275
And they, Yes. No one can
get sober for their jobs,

00:01:26.275 --> 00:01:29.140
for their wife, for their kids.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.710
They can't do it for any of that.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.420
They could only do it when
they decide their done.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.675
Truthfully.

00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:36.508
- And that's hard.

00:01:36.508 --> 00:01:39.845
- I mean it's kind of
radical to think about.

00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:40.678
You know what I mean.

00:01:40.678 --> 00:01:42.567
And you think "I love them so much,

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:43.587
"why can't they do it for me?

00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:44.697
"Or they're going to lose their job.

00:01:44.697 --> 00:01:45.664
"Don't they understand?"

00:01:45.664 --> 00:01:47.680
Until that light goes on,

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.420
there's honestly not much you can do.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.253
- That's when its a disease though.

00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:52.400
- When the light goes on there is hope.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.340
When the light goes on,

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.154
absolutely there's definitely

00:01:55.154 --> 00:01:56.970
a great life beyond it for sure.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.405
- Thank you so much for
being so open about it

00:01:58.405 --> 00:02:00.380
because seriously not everybody is,

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.700
and we all struggle with stuff .

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.420
And I think that people that go through it

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.540
and friends of mines that go through it,

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.450
its nice to know you're not alone.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.624
The best part is to know
you're not on some like island

00:02:09.624 --> 00:02:11.485
like screwing up your life.

00:02:11.485 --> 00:02:12.318
- There's hope!

00:02:12.318 --> 00:02:13.200
- We're all on a island
screwing up our lives.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.900
- My life is 100 times more,

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.430
my big worry when I got sober was

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.870
I wasn't going to have fun anymore.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.720
I was young. I was 26.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.696
I was like I'm not giving up my fun.

00:02:22.696 --> 00:02:23.845
I could never imagine.

00:02:23.845 --> 00:02:26.390
So when I get married I'm
not going to have a drink.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.920
When I have a kid, I'm not
going to have a whiskey.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.953
Guess what yes. I didn't have
any of that and its awesome.

